{"title":"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 20","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Alcumus)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Alcumus)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Select numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> independently and at random, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be their sum. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/f/bef747a48a2a8d43c4841e12c89f2de2502a672e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A, B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the results when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/3/3834f0cef2a1f4d8524aa5bc8e3faca298550862.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"25\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, respectively, are rounded to the nearest integer. What is the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Probability\" title=\"Probability\">probability</a> that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/3/1d3d99747227e632f73e535a91acaac5526825ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A + B = C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"89\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/0/b2073745bd8e74d06c71a90b3b0cfffd9e832e6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text {(A)}\\ \\frac14 \\qquad \\text {(B)}\\ \\frac13 \\qquad \\text {(C)}\\ \\frac12 \\qquad \\text {(D)}\\ \\frac23 \\qquad \\text {(E)}\\ \\frac34$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"349\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Casework\" title=\"Casework\">Casework</a>:\n</p>\n<ol><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/7/fe74e7ca51b767bc13e0e0cd53e58e5800de01b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 + 0 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />. The probability that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/8/a689cea3a462529e80c535f6a136415467a822a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a &lt; \\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"49\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/4/7f48e067b6ed915c30d5f09181e7c54ae3912d18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b &lt; \\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"43\" height=\"37\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/7/62702114499f41b4dd5f0858d29ce49e7112cf6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac 12\\right)^2 = \\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"82\" height=\"46\" />. Notice that the sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add2609af1bb7632cc22b68fd49fdd94de06b327.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" /> ranges from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> with a symmetric distribution across <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/6/e86c22d83ea01eb477116a1414a9adb33f5cbc4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b=c=\\frac 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"107\" height=\"37\" />, and we want <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/e/f5e3bc115262648447eaae2cd7df5314b8bb82cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c &lt; \\frac 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"43\" height=\"37\" />. Thus the chance is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/c/70cdd6f508ad2154563a4f188b4689b03778f97c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\frac{1}{4}}2 = \\frac 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"50\" height=\"40\" />.</li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/4/ff4783cf49551c2d97df6a2f98006089c5938fa3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 + 1 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"14\" />. The probability that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/b/84b1f7185e790c58926a7ea111524a1388799932.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a &lt; \\frac 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"49\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/9/f99a057e418b97d4c51600ff198b1b6bbdc0a488.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b &gt; \\frac 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"43\" height=\"37\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/d/14d48fb052d7fa270cfe6d5a0b5ef1f1cb1c2ad1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />, but now <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/9/139e38b2333e6d2728e543237c387e57e768888c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} &lt; a+b = c &lt; \\frac 32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"145\" height=\"37\" />, which makes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/e/77e3435fdaadad9195048f672956b8e6bef8db23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" /> automatically. Hence the chance is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/d/14d48fb052d7fa270cfe6d5a0b5ef1f1cb1c2ad1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />.</li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/6/586e64c2b6aebf903e473aa7f46f730d232ab6b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 0 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"14\" />. This is the same as the previous case.</li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/9/349b6b8a00581fb06095c20113d8fa49f3f5cf9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 1 = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"13\" />. We recognize that this is equivalent to the first case.</li></ol>\n<p>Our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/7/997497fba04318b01f1a6a17dafaaf08dd70e985.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\left(\\frac 18 + \\frac 14 \\right) = \\frac 34 \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{(E)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"177\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Use areas to deal with this continuous probability problem. Set up a unit square with values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> on x-axis and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> on y-axis.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/e/efea22aeb207eeb0b1544fb0ab814ca5a1752ba0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b &lt; 1/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"90\" height=\"18\" /> then this will work because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/6/036eaaa5ac4842d013f88736c4e5df9eacd01e9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = B = C = 0$\" width=\"124\" height=\"13\" />. Similarly if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/c/5acbf5e7f35784b085597153f77ee3c46c541bea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b &gt; 3/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"90\" height=\"18\" /> then this will work because in order for this to happen, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are each greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/3/1f3cc0ad966b3e637cd199607cbf0d1befc0e491.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"29\" height=\"20\" /> making <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/7/917f20abc977fee360d76a224e6e8529f03e2a79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = B = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"85\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/d/13d38e76d7d5fcfc00ea546b2219585c058823e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C = 2$\" width=\"47\" height=\"12\" />. Each of these triangles in the unit square has area of 1/8.\n</p><p>The only case left is when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/e/77e3435fdaadad9195048f672956b8e6bef8db23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" />. Then each of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> must be 1 and 0, in any order. These cut off squares of area 1/2 from the upper left and lower right corners of the unit square.\n</p><p>Then the area producing the desired result is 3/4. Since the area of the unit square is 1, the probability is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/1/d21715ef3fb94d12fc089969a648efb480cd5b6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac 34$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"11\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Alcumus.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Alcumus)\">Solution 3 (Alcumus)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Alcumus)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The conditions under which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/f/b6f8667d5ede6d39e5af95a81aadc0c3a61937d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A+B=C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"89\" height=\"14\" /> are as follows.\n</p><p><br />\n(i) If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/c/6acaa11e50950df9a3a938d640dab11727d078e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b&lt; 1/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"90\" height=\"18\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/7/687bc4e28a225479eb751d63f7be66c7d272164b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=B=C=0$\" width=\"124\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n(ii) If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/2/7a2827d65534a43222b8582453a443da00d0bddf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\geq 1/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/2/972888db0e864da3324d21fa944a17de2aa5787c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&lt;1/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/5/33535d13e10f27c6657f5795ecb46f5c415ad539.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B=0$\" width=\"47\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/d/b0df689f7b71732bf9c92a83b15675d456d38b5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=C=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"84\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n(iii) If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/1/cd164660eb39c13e5ddcc7b3e4b1cc52644c5246.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&lt;1/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/6/896f1ce5e7d5efa3f35e27e852bc91fb6d2fe8f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b\\geq 1/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/4/9f44a5278f9f07028b5386312e86885738ffec92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=0$\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/8/198c836cb64ef984c459716bc559949793d6e941.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B=C=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"85\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n(iv) If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/7/17749631054c458bb400506b576e92121a685580.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b\\geq 3/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"90\" height=\"18\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/c/34cc0ee4399c5595afef4d0992fb46828805584f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=B=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"85\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/a/80a86e1acaed1861bcef6fa6dd99b5c3db29b537.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C=2$\" width=\"47\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>These conditions correspond to the shaded regions of the graph shown. The combined area of those regions is 3/4, and the area of the entire square is 1, so the requested probability is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/b/3ab531643dc2a5466e9d447e752f2c6181b9d048.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{3/4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"39\" height=\"29\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0619188c95a19aaaf8ddafd4a3144933f53dde03.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(2cm); draw((1.1,0)--(0,0)--(0,1.1),linewidth(1)); fill((0,0)--(1,0)--(1,1)--(0,1)--cycle,gray(0.7)); fill((0.5,0)--(0.5,0.5)--(0,0.5)--cycle,white); fill((0.5,0.5)--(1,0.5)--(0.5,1)--cycle,white); label(&quot;$a$&quot;,(1.1,0),E); label(&quot;$b$&quot;,(0,1.1),N); label(&quot;1&quot;,(1,0),S); label(&quot;1&quot;,(0,1),W); label(&quot;0&quot;,(0,0),SW); [/asy]\" width=\"142\" height=\"148\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A\">2004 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 19\">Problem 19</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 21\">Problem 21</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</